WHAT THIS IS

Blossom's source code is published so that anybody can read it and check
what the app actually does with their data. That is the whole reason it is
public. It is not open source, and this licence does not pretend to be an
open source licence.

You may:

  - Read, study and audit this code, in full, for any purpose.
  - Copy it locally and run it on your own machine to verify what it does.
  - Quote from it, write about it, and point at it in a security or privacy
    review.
  - Submit changes back to Grey Studios.

You may not, without written permission from Grey Studios:

  - Run this software, or anything derived from it, as a service for anyone
    other than yourself.
  - Distribute it, publish it, or make it available to other people, whether
    modified or not.
  - Sell it, or include it in anything you sell.
  - Use the Blossom name, the Blossom flower mark, or Grey Studios branding
    for anything other than referring to this project.

WHY IT IS THIS WAY

Blossom holds some of the most sensitive information a person has. Anybody
running a copy of it under a similar name would be trusted by users who
believed they were using Blossom, and Grey Studios would have no way to
know what that copy did with their data. Reading the code costs nothing and
protects nobody's privacy but proves ours; running unaccountable copies is
a different thing entirely.

If you want to do something this licence does not allow, ask. The answer is
often yes.

